  "hints": [
    "Nothing is assumed about n, so split into cases: n even and n odd.",
    "In each case, write 5n² + 3n + 7 as 2·(integer) + 1 and give that integer as the case's witness."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Case $n = 2k$: $5n^2 + 3n + 7 = 20k^2 + 6k + 7 = 2(10k^2 + 3k + 3) + 1$, which is odd.",
    "Case $n = 2k + 1$: $5n^2 + 3n + 7 = 20k^2 + 26k + 15 = 2(10k^2 + 13k + 7) + 1$, which is odd.",
    "Every integer is even or odd, so $5n^2 + 3n + 7$ is always odd. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
